### Layout

```
├── .agents/            # shared AI agent instructions (coding conventions, PR/task checklists, project structure)
├── .github/            # GitHub-specific config (workflows, issue/PR templates)
├── .vscode/            # VS Code editor/workspace settings
├── api/                # OpenAPI/Swagger specs, JSON schemas, protocol definitions
├── assets/             # repository assets (images, logos, etc)
├── config/             # global application configuration
├── deployments/        # deployment configs and templates (docker-compose, kubernetes/helm, terraform)
├── docs/               # design and user documents
├── examples/           # examples for applications and/or public libraries
├── packages/           # workspace packages for a monorepo (npm/yarn/pnpm/bun workspaces)
├── scripts/            # build/install/analysis scripts (keeps package.json scripts small)
├── src/                # application/library source code (default entrypoint: main.ts)
├── test/               # additional external test apps, fixtures, and test data
├── web/                # web app components: static assets, server-side templates, SPAs
├── .editorconfig       # editor formatting rules
├── .gitignore          # git ignore patterns
├── .npmrc              # npm/pnpm package-manager config (registry, install, publish settings)
├── .yarnrc.yml         # yarn config (yarn berry; yarn classic uses .yarnrc)
├── AGENTS.md           # instructions for AI coding agents
├── CLAUDE.md           # instructions specific for Claude coding agents
├── CONTRIBUTING.md     # contribution guidelines
├── Dockerfile          # container build definition
├── Makefile            # build/test/lint task automation (optional)
├── bun.lock            # bun dependency lockfile
├── bunfig.toml         # bun package-manager and runtime config
├── package.json        # package manifest: scripts, dependencies, and workspaces (npm/yarn/bun)
├── package-lock.json   # npm dependency lockfile
├── pnpm-lock.yaml      # pnpm dependency lockfile
├── pnpm-workspace.yaml # pnpm workspace configuration (workspace globs, settings)
├── tsconfig.json       # TypeScript compiler options
├── yarn.lock           # yarn dependency lockfile
<!-- Project-specific / Layout -->
```

### Layer Dependencies

Notes for declaring layers in the `Layer Dependencies` section of `.attunic/context.md`; adjust them to the project before declaring.

- `src/main.ts` (or the framework entrypoint) is the outermost layer: parse env/config, wire dependencies, then delegate to `src/` modules; it may import everything, and nothing imports it.
- Layers live under `src/`, organized by responsibility (e.g. `src/auth/`, `src/http/`), not by type; one suggestion, innermost first:

| Layer | Typical path | Depends on | Must never contain |
|-------|--------------|------------|--------------------|
| domain | src/\<area\>/domain | itself | framework types, database, HTTP |
| application | src/\<area\>/application | domain | database access, HTTP handlers |
| adapter | src/\<area\>/http, src/\<area\>/cli | application, domain | SQL, external clients |
| infrastructure | src/\<area\>/infrastructure | application (its ports), domain | business rules |

- Prefer passing dependencies in (constructor injection) over module-level singletons, so a layer boundary can be substituted in tests.
- Check by hand: read the imports of changed files; an inner module importing an outer one is a violation.
